## 6. AI Generation Rules

### Generate

[What an AI agent can produce from this L3 spec:]
- [e.g., Screen layouts for all steps in the flow logic]
- [e.g., Component assembly for each screen using referenced L2 specs]
- [e.g., Form validation logic for all validated inputs]
- [e.g., Transition animations between steps]
- [e.g., Error and empty state screens per edge cases section]

### Validate

[What the agent must check before approving output:]
- [ ] All components in generated output appear in section 3 Components Used
- [ ] All components are assembled per their ACTIVE L2 specs (state by state)
- [ ] All steps in section 4 are represented in the generated flow
- [ ] All edge cases in section 5 have generated handling
- [ ] No component in output references a DRAFT or STALE L2 spec
- [ ] No custom tokens, raw values, or off-spec components appear

### Forbidden

[What the agent must never generate:]
- Components not listed in section 3
- Flow steps not in section 4 (no assumed steps)
- Edge case handling that contradicts section 5 specifications
- Custom token values or off-token styling
- [Flow-specific forbidden items]

### Prompt Seed

```
Generate the [Flow Name] for [Product Name].

Reference: SDDn Delivery Spec [FLOW-L3-NNN] v[version].

Component specs in scope (all ACTIVE):
[List each: Component Name — spec_id vX.X.X]

Required output:
- All [N] steps in the flow logic (section 4)
- Edge case handling for all [N] cases (section 5)
- Use only components listed in section 3, in the variants and states defined in their L2 specs

Constraints from parent L1 [SYSTEM-L1-NNN]:
- [Key L1 constraint relevant to this flow]
- [Accessibility requirement]

Do not generate: steps or components outside this spec.
```

---

## 7. Definition of Done

[Testable criteria for the complete delivery. Distinct from L2 Acceptance Criteria (per-component). This covers the assembled flow.]

**Functional:**
- [ ] Happy path completes end-to-end without errors in staging environment
- [ ] All [N] steps render with correct data and components
- [ ] [Business-specific completion criterion]

**Edge cases:**
- [ ] All [N] edge cases in section 5 tested and handled per spec
- [ ] Network error during submission shows error state and allows retry
- [ ] [Additional edge case test]

**Accessibility:**
- [ ] Keyboard navigation completes full flow without mouse
- [ ] No WCAG 2.2 AA violations in automated scan
- [ ] Screen reader announces all state changes

**Quality:**
- [ ] No DRAFT or STALE L2 spec referenced in delivered components
- [ ] No raw token values in delivered implementation
- [ ] PO sign-off: flow logic matches business intent
- [ ] QA regression: no impact on adjacent flows

---

## 8. Validation Checklist

[For the spec reviewer. Distinct from Definition of Done (which is for the implementer).]

**Spec quality:**
- [ ] All components in section 3 have ACTIVE L2 specs
- [ ] Flow logic covers all entry points in section 2
- [ ] All edge cases have explicit, specific handling (not "show an error")
- [ ] AI Generation Rules do not contradict referenced L2 rules
- [ ] Definition of Done is fully testable

**Content:**
- [ ] Intent aligns with approved product requirements
- [ ] User Context matches current persona / segment definition
- [ ] Copy in flow logic matches approved voice and tone (per L1 Brand Constraints)

**Inheritance:**
- [ ] All L2 spec versions in section 9 match section 3
- [ ] No referenced L2 is in STALE or DEPRECATED state

